---
layout: layouts/base.njk
pagination:
  data: catalog.sectors
  size: 1
  alias: sector
  addAllPagesToCollections: true
permalink: "/sectors/{{ sector.slug }}/"
eleventyComputed:
  pageId: "sectors-{{ sector.slug }}"
  title: "{{ sector.name | safe }} — Sector dossier"
  description: "{{ sector.id }} {{ sector.name }}: what the sector includes, where AI and robotics could reduce costs, the guardrails, and the honest evidence status."
---
{#-
  One design for all 15 sector dossiers (design-source/pages/sectors/*.html).

  DESIGN: structure, classes and section order from the export. The hero
  geometry is load-bearing — .sector-title / .sector-sub min-heights and the
  .sector-illus-slot offset hold the illustration at an identical Y on all 15;
  removing any of them reintroduces the drift the export warns about.

  CONTENT: every field comes from the repository's own dossier
  (sectors/SEC-0NN-*.md via _data/catalog.js) and _data/sectorContent.js — never
  from the export's draft sectors.json. Sector names are canonical: always in
  full, never abbreviated. A field the dossier does not carry renders a visible
  [CONTENT NEEDED] marker rather than filler.
-#}
{% from "partials/content-needed.njk" import block as gap, inline as gapInline %}
{% import "partials/figure.njk" as fig %}
{% set sc = sectorContent[sector.slug] %}
{% set headlineRow = register.byId[sc.headlineSrc] if sc.headlineSrc else null %}
{#- Related sectors: the next three in canonical order, wrapping. Mechanical,
    so no editorial judgement is invented per sector. -#}
{% set sqColours = ["bg-ink-blue", "bg-clay", "bg-coral"] %}

<!-- SECTION: sectors/{{ sector.slug }}.Sector head -->
<section class="sector-head" data-screen-label="Sector head">
  <div class="breadcrumb"><a href="/">Uncost</a> &nbsp;/&nbsp; <a href="/sectors/">Sectors</a> &nbsp;/&nbsp; <span>{{ sector.name }}</span></div>
  <div class="sector-head-grid">
    <div>
      <h1 class="sector-title">{{ sector.name }}.</h1>
      <p class="sector-sub">{% if sector.includes %}{{ sector.includes }}{% else %}{{ gapInline("sector-includes") }}{% endif %}</p>
      <div class="sector-num"><span class="nb">Sector <b>{{ sector.num }} / 15</b></span> &middot; <span class="nb"><span class="status status--{{ sector.statusClass }}">{{ sector.status }}</span></span> &middot; <span class="nb">Dossier <b>{{ sector.id }}</b></span></div>
    </div>
    <div class="sector-illus-slot">{% image sector.illustration.src, sector.illustration.alt, "(max-width: 920px) 90vw, 460px", [280, 620, 1024] %}</div>
  </div>
</section>

<nav class="anchor-bar" aria-label="Page sections">
  <a href="#scope">Scope &amp; opportunity <span class="cnt">01</span></a>
  <a href="#evidence">Evidence status <span class="cnt">02</span></a>
  <a href="#worked">Worked example <span class="cnt">03</span></a>
  {% if sector.relatedProjects.length %}<a href="#projects">Related projects <span class="cnt">04</span></a>{% endif %}
  <a href="#sources">Sources <span class="cnt">{% if sector.relatedProjects.length %}05{% else %}04{% endif %}</span></a>
</nav>

<!-- SECTION: sectors/{{ sector.slug }}.Scope -->
<section id="scope" class="block block--ink bt-0" data-screen-label="Scope">
  <div class="eyebrow">01 &middot; Scope, opportunity, guardrail</div>
  <h2>Where automation could bite &mdash; and what stays visible.</h2>
  <div class="scope">
    <div><h3><i></i>What it includes</h3><p>{% if sector.includes %}{{ sector.includes }}{% else %}{{ gapInline("sector-includes") }}{% endif %}</p></div>
    <div><h3><i></i>The opportunity</h3><p>{% if sector.opportunity %}{{ sector.opportunity }}{% else %}{{ gapInline("sector-opportunity") }}{% endif %}</p></div>
    <div><h3><i></i>The guardrail</h3><p>{% if sector.guardrail %}{{ sector.guardrail }}{% else %}{{ gapInline("sector-guardrail") }}{% endif %}</p></div>
  </div>
  <p class="note-on-ink">Roadmap status: <b class="t-cream">{{ sector.status }}</b> &mdash; status is sequencing, not importance.</p>
</section>

<!-- SECTION: sectors/{{ sector.slug }}.Evidence status -->
<section id="evidence" class="block block--ink" data-screen-label="Evidence status">
  <div class="eyebrow">02 &middot; Evidence status</div>
  <h2>No number ships without a <span class="t-coral">receipt</span>.</h2>
  {% if headlineRow %}
  <div class="evd-empty">
    {{ fig.stat(headlineRow) }}
    <p>Every figure on this page carries: value, unit, region, date observed, a source ID from the public register, a confidence label, and the collection method.</p>
    <div class="chip-row">
      <span class="rcpt-conf rcpt-conf--confirmed">Confirmed</span>
      <span class="rcpt-conf rcpt-conf--estimate">Estimate</span>
      <span class="rcpt-conf rcpt-conf--scenario">Scenario</span>
      <span class="rcpt-conf rcpt-conf--needs-refresh">Needs refresh</span>
    </div>
  </div>
  {% else %}
  <div class="evd-empty">
    {% if sector.evidence %}<h3>{{ sector.evidence }}</h3>{% else %}{{ gap("sector-evidence") }}{% endif %}
    <p>Reviewed source records come before figures. When the first {{ sector.name }} figures publish, each line will carry: value, unit, region, date observed, a source ID from the public register, a confidence label, and the collection method.</p>
    <div class="chip-row">
      <span class="rcpt-conf rcpt-conf--confirmed">Confirmed</span>
      <span class="rcpt-conf rcpt-conf--estimate">Estimate</span>
      <span class="rcpt-conf rcpt-conf--scenario">Scenario</span>
      <span class="rcpt-conf rcpt-conf--needs-refresh">Needs refresh</span>
    </div>
  </div>
  {% endif %}
  <div class="rcpt-row rcpt-row-on-ink"><span class="rcpt-src t-on-ink-2"><b class="t-on-ink-2">Register</b>sources/register.csv &mdash; public on GitHub</span><span class="rcpt-updated">Checked {{ register.lastChecked }}</span></div>
</section>

<!-- SECTION: sectors/{{ sector.slug }}.Worked example -->
<section id="worked" class="block" data-screen-label="Worked example">
  {% if sc.workedExample.measurement %}
  <div class="eyebrow">03 &middot; Where the method stops</div>
  <h2>How far the method goes in {{ sector.name }} &mdash; and where it stops.</h2>
  <p class="prose-60">Nothing below is a finding. It is what the work would look like &mdash; up to the point where it must stop.</p>
  <div class="steps6">
    {% for step in sc.workedExample.steps %}
    <div class="step6"><div class="n">{{ loop.index }}</div><div><p>{{ step }}</p></div></div>
    {% endfor %}
  </div>
  <p class="prose-60"><b>Then we stop.</b> Steps 4 to 6 &mdash; matching a mechanism, packaging it for others to run, and tracking whether the cost falls &mdash; would put a tool between a person and their {{ sc.workedExample.stopBetween }}. That needs {{ sc.workedExample.stopReason }} &mdash; and none of that exists yet. Until it does, {{ sector.name }} is a measurement sector: we can show what it costs and where the cost sits. We will not package something for a community group to run.</p>
  {% else %}
  <div class="eyebrow">03 &middot; How a {{ sector.name | lower }} cost gets uncosted</div>
  <h2>{{ sc.workedExample.scenario }}</h2>
  <p class="prose-60">Nothing below is a finding. It is what the work would look like, step by step.</p>
  <div class="steps6">
    {% for step in sc.workedExample.steps %}
    <div class="step6"><div class="n">{{ loop.index }}</div><div><p>{{ step }}</p></div></div>
    {% endfor %}
  </div>
  {% endif %}
</section>

{% if sector.guardrail %}
<!-- SECTION: sectors/{{ sector.slug }}.Guardrail callout -->
<section class="callout" data-screen-label="Guardrail callout">
  <blockquote>&ldquo;{{ sector.guardrail }}&rdquo;</blockquote>
  <div class="attr">&mdash; The {{ sector.name }} guardrail &middot; dossier {{ sector.id }}</div>
</section>
{% endif %}

{% if sector.relatedProjects.length %}
<!-- SECTION: sectors/{{ sector.slug }}.Related projects -->
<section id="projects" class="block block--cream2 bt-0" data-screen-label="Related projects">
  <div class="eyebrow">04 &middot; Related projects</div>
  <h2>Where {{ sector.name }} shows up in The Projects.</h2>
  <table class="prj-table">
    <thead><tr><th>ID</th><th>Project</th><th>Role for {{ sector.name }}</th><th>Status</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
    {% for p in sector.relatedProjects %}
      <tr>
        <td class="id">{{ p.id }}</td>
        <td class="title"><a href="/projects/{{ p.slug }}/">{{ p.display }}</a><span class="sum">{{ p.line }}</span></td>
        <td class="role">{% if p.layer %}{{ p.layer }}{% else %}{{ p.tag | capitalize }}{% endif %}</td>
        <td><span class="status status--planned">Draft &mdash; not approved for build</span></td>
      </tr>
    {% endfor %}
    </tbody>
  </table>
</section>
{% endif %}

<!-- SECTION: sectors/{{ sector.slug }}.Sources -->
<section id="sources" class="block" data-screen-label="Sources">
  <div class="eyebrow">{% if sector.relatedProjects.length %}05{% else %}04{% endif %} &middot; Sources</div>
  <h2>The register comes before the figures.</h2>
  <p class="prose-60">Every source Uncost uses gets a public ID, publisher, date, licence, refresh cadence and region coverage. The {{ sector.name }} dossier draws on the register as reviewed records are added.</p>
  {% if headlineRow %}
  <div class="src" data-source="{{ headlineRow.source_id }}"><div class="src-num">{{ headlineRow.source_id }}</div><div class="src-body"><a href="/receipts/#{{ headlineRow.source_id }}">{{ headlineRow.title }}</a><span class="meta">{{ headlineRow.publisher }} &middot; {{ headlineRow.publication_date }} &middot; confidence: {{ headlineRow.confidence }}</span></div></div>
  {% endif %}
  <div class="src" data-source="SRC-001"><div class="src-num">SRC-001</div><div class="src-body"><a href="https://github.com/uncost-org/uncost/blob/main/sources/register.csv" target="_blank" rel="noopener">{{ register.byId["SRC-001"].title }}</a><span class="meta">Governance-control source &middot; {{ register.byId["SRC-001"].publication_date }} &middot; confidence: {{ register.byId["SRC-001"].confidence }}</span></div></div>
  <div class="src bb-soft"><div class="src-num">&mdash;</div><div class="src-body">Sector-specific source records are added with review. <a href="https://github.com/uncost-org/uncost" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Propose a source on GitHub</a><span class="meta">Official statistics first &middot; licences recorded at intake</span></div></div>
</section>

<!-- SECTION: sectors/{{ sector.slug }}.Related sectors -->
<section class="block block--cream2" data-screen-label="Related sectors">
  <div class="eyebrow">Related sectors</div>
  <h2>Keep reading.</h2>
  <div class="related">
    {% for offset in [1, 2, 3] %}
    {% set neighbour = catalog.sectors[(loop.index0 + sector.num | int) % 15] %}
    <a href="/sectors/{{ neighbour.slug }}/"><span class="sq {{ sqColours[loop.index0] }}"></span> {{ neighbour.name }}</a>
    {% endfor %}
    <a class="bd-dashed" href="/sectors/"><span class="sq sq-outline"></span> All 15 sectors &rarr;</a>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- SECTION: sectors/{{ sector.slug }}.Sector CTA -->
<section class="block block--ink" data-screen-label="Sector CTA">
  <h2 class="sec-cta">Help build the {{ sector.name | lower }} evidence.<br><span class="t-coral">Sources before slogans.</span></h2>
  <p class="lead-on-ink">Early useful roles: {{ sc.ctaRoles | join(", ") }} &mdash; and, as the work grows, a volunteer {{ sector.name }} sector lead.</p>
  <div class="row-16">
    <a href="/join/" class="u-btn u-btn--primary">Take part</a>
    <a href="https://github.com/uncost-org/uncost" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="u-btn u-btn--outline-cream">The public records</a>
  </div>
</section>
